  "legacyDialogue": [
    {
      "speaker": "Dain",
      "portrait": "warden",
      "text": "The households are meeting in the northern village. I will tell them why my patrol fought the wrong people."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "The branch carries the woodcutters’ memory. The Rootbinder would rather burn it than let their families listen."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "Take the bridge fort so the villagers can cross safely. Lark can use whichever path gets her to the meeting alive."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Tamsin",
      "portrait": "adept",
      "text": "Dain sent for me. Some of those woodcutters were my neighbors. I will help clear your road; their families need the truth, not another duel with their master."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "The branch has flowered. The households have heard what happened beneath the grove."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "And the fort is ours. No one must ask the overseer’s leave to cross this river again."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "We will keep the road open together. The Rootbinder can hide from us, but he cannot hide the truth now."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Tamsin",
      "portrait": "adept",
      "text": "The households are meeting in the northern village. I saw the grove’s memory; I will stand beside you when they hear it."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "The households have heard the woodcutters. Dain is among the names we must remember, too."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "The fort is ours and the meeting has chosen an open road. That is a promise we can still keep."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "Then let the first travelers cross. We have enough graves; we need neighbors."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "Someone left these for a traveler who never came. Today, someone will."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Dain",
      "portrait": "warden",
      "text": "Lark carries a living branch. When it flowers, no one can pretend the grove was only lumber."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "It will flower. But I would rather not test that while a skeleton is shooting at me."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "Secure the bridge. The witness comes first. Dain, your spears and our boars hold the open road together."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Tamsin",
      "portrait": "adept",
      "text": "The dead hardly feel arrows, but stone sparks crack bone. Let the shields hold them while I work. Lark can rest in the groves beyond the ford."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "It flowered."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Dain",
      "portrait": "warden",
      "text": "Then I will say what I saw. And I will keep saying it until they hear."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "Leave the bridge open. That is what a pact is for."
    }
  ]
